            "review_title": "Review at IKRA Restaurant My An - Slavic cuisine",
            "review_text": "Hilts\nDa Nang, Vietnam533 contributions\n4\nDelicious home cooked food from the motherland\nJul 2026 • Friends\nIf you’re missing some good, home-cooked food from the motherland, I recommend you visit IKRA.\n\nService:\n- The young ladies who greeted me, took my order and delivered my food were friendly, polite, and always smiling 🤗\n- My food was delivered in 12 minutes.\n- They replenished the complimentary water, which was greatly appreciated.\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nAtmosphere:\n- Overall, I really liked the vibe.\n- Nice decor in line with the restaurant's theme.\n- The seats are comfortable.\n- The lighting is nice.\n- They have an open kitchen.\n- The table decorations were cute.\n- The air conditioning wasn’t too cold.\n- They also played some nice background music.\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nMy Order:\n- 1 x Potato Pancake with Salmon and Cucumber. Served with Sour Cream.\n- Everything was fresh and tasted delicious.\n- Price: 155K\n- Rating: 5/5\n\n- 1 x Lingonberry & BlackBerry Meringue Pie Classic\n- Absolutely Delicious 😋\n- Fresh berries, fluffy meringue, and good pastry.\n- Price: 95K\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nAdditional information:\n- Overall, I would say the prices are reasonable.\n- They provided a bottle of complimentary water.\n- The toilet was clean and had tissue and soap.\n\nSome feedback for the owner:\n- It’s a shame the main courses are only available between 15:00 and 21:30.\n\nOverall rating: 5/5\n\nCongratulations Anastasia and team on opening a beautiful business that serves delicious, authentic food in a lovely atmosphere with great service 👏 👏 👏\nRead more\nWritten September 21, 2026",
